# Shell scripts are checked out LF on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows development machine, so git stores
# LF and checks out CRLF. bash tolerates that under Git Bash and does not
# under WSL, and build/mips/endian_gate.sh is the one file in this tree
# that hands itself to WSL - its wsl.exe call re-runs the script from
# /mnt/e, where the backslash-continued condition at line 74 stops being
# a continuation:
#
#   build/mips/endian_gate.sh: line 75: syntax error near unexpected token `&&'
#
# Reproduced with WSL's bash -n, which needs no MIPS toolchain to reach
# the parse: the gate's own SKIP path runs fine under Git Bash, so the
# failure only ever shows up after the WSL hand-off has already happened.
#
# ONLY .sh IS NAMED HERE, and the scope is a measurement rather than a
# convention: endian_gate.sh is the only wsl.exe call site in build/,
# gates.mk and the Makefile (grepped), so .sh is the only file type any
# WSL path parses. Nothing else in the tree is executed that way, and an
# eol stated for a type nothing parses that way would be a rule with no
# measurement behind it. There are no .bat or .cmd files to protect in
# the other direction.
*.sh text eol=lf
